# SES → BA degree completion: nested-specification analysis (n = 8773, 236 events, base rate 2.69%)

## Answer
**SES (socioeconomic status).** Its logit coefficient on BA-degree completion falls from
**+0.3524** (race already in, before academic characteristics) / **+0.4729** (SES alone) to
**−0.2316** once BOTH race and academic characteristics (ABILITY, PERCENTILE IN CLASS) are in,
and it stops being significant at the 1% level (p < 0.00001 → p = 0.0211).

## Headline table (logit, log-odds, SES in native units; per-SD column in parentheses)
| model | block added | beta | SE | p | 95% CI | OR | sig@1% | sig@5% |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| M1  | SES only | +0.4729 | 0.0826 | <1e-5 | [0.311, 0.635] | 1.605 | yes | yes |
