Per-SD (z) mirror: 0.3511 → 0.2616 → −0.1611 → −0.1720 → −0.1766.

## Block attribution (delta beta from M1)
race alone −0.1205 · academic alone −0.6900 · both −0.7045 → **~98% of the drop is the academic block.**
Disaggregated: +ABILITY only → −0.2306 (sign already flipped); +PCTILE only → +0.0814 (p = 0.372,
positive, insignificant); +race+PCTILE → −0.0025 (p = 0.972).

## Anchor reproduction (no cherry-picking)
Exhaustive search: 64 covariate subsets × 2 scales = 128 fits; 5888 ordered spec pairs under one
free scale multiplier. Best **nested** pair that genuinely adds the academic block:
`SES+race (0.3524)` → `SES+race+academic (−0.2316)`, multiplier 1.0317, joint error 0.0097
(|0.3524−0.3636| = 0.0112 and |−0.2316+0.2293| = 0.0023). Raw log-odds scale is the best fit;
no multiplier of exactly 1.0 reproduces both anchors, so the source's SES is ~3% differently scaled.

## Uniqueness
Of 7 candidates × 2 scales, **only SES** changes sign + → − across the ladder
(SES raw 0.4729 → −0.2379; SES z 0.3511 → −0.1766). Race dummies do move toward zero
(BLACK −0.8757 → +0.1411, p = 0.530; HISP −0.7222 → −0.1778, p = 0.479) but never start positive.
SEX_F is never significant (0.2037, p = 0.125 → 0.2128, p = 0.131). ABILITY, PCTILE, FAMSIZE
are large and rock-stable.

## Collinearity / suppression
VIF in M4: SES 1.327, SEX_F 1.312, BLACK 1.327, HISP 1.187, ABILITY 2.477, PCTILE 2.012;
condition number 4.26. corr(SES,ABILITY)=0.463, corr(SES,PCTILE)=0.304.
The sign flip is driven by ABILITY (VIF low), so it is **substantive suppression/mediation, not a
collinearity artefact** — but the sign IS unstable across academic covariates (PCTILE alone leaves
SES positive), so the negative sign is specifically an ABILITY-conditional statement.

## Robustness
Firth penalised logit (rare events): 0.3501 → 0.2605 → −0.1622 → −0.1734 → −0.1781 — identical
pattern, conclusions unchanged. LPM/OLS ruled out on scale: max |slope| 0.029, theoretical ceiling
for a 0/1 predictor ≈ base rate 0.027, so 0.3636 cannot be a raw probability coefficient.

## Limitations
1. "Insignificant" holds at α = 0.01 (p = 0.021); at α = 0.05 the coefficient is still marginally
   significant. SE needed for p > 0.05 at −0.2316 would be 0.118 vs realised 0.1005.
2. The `curriculum` covariate promised by the dataset description is absent from the file; the
   academic block is therefore only ABILITY + PERCENTILE.
3. Exact source values not reproduced to the digit → source likely used a slightly different SES
   scaling and/or an extra covariate. Direction, magnitude, sign change and significance loss are reproduced.
4. Race coefficients are imprecise (Black n=2113/28 events); the mediation claim for the race block
   is weak. M5 (adding FAMILY SIZE) makes SES positive again (β_z = +0.2158) — the SES sign is
   specification-sensitive and is only negative in the race+academic conditioning set.
